# Customer-facing copy (Acorns Nest landing site)

Write like the existing homepage: directors and owners reading on a busy day. Match `HERO`, `CTA`, and `STORY_SECTIONS` in `src/lib/content.ts`.

## Do

- Short sentences. Plain words. Contractions when the rest of the site uses them.
- Name real product bits (Bulk Log, Menu Planner, walkthrough) when relevant.
- Canadian spelling: centre, licence (as licensed), behaviour only if already used elsewhere.
- Say what is true about pilot scope (Atlantic Canada) without sounding like a press release.

## Do not (AI / marketing watermarks)

- Em dashes (—) in user-visible strings. Use a period or comma instead.
- Phrases like: pilot terms, onboarding, tailored/shaped to, where it makes sense, leverage, robust, seamless, game-changer, delighted, excited to announce, centre by centre (unless the user asks for it).
- Long chains: "rooms, staff, and parent communication — and pilot centres…"
- Generic quote CTAs: "Contact us for a quote", "Go to contact form", "put together pilot pricing".
- Support lines that read like a policy footer: "Billing questions go to… Monday to Friday, Atlantic time" unless the user wants exact hours in that tone.

## Checks before shipping copy

- Read it aloud once. If it sounds like a SaaS blog post, rewrite shorter.
- No em dashes in `content.ts`, page metadata descriptions, or visible JSX text.
